---
title: The Vigil: At the Eucharist
type: acclamation
citation: BCP 294
bulletin: full
---

[Rubric] *The candles at the Altar may now be lighted from the Paschal Candle.*
[Rubric] *One of the following Canticles is then sung. Immediately before the Canticle the Celebrant may say to the people*
[Celebrant] Alleluia. Christ is risen.
[People] **The Lord is risen indeed. Alleluia.**

---

# The Canticles

[Rubric] *Gloria in excelsis Te Deum laudamus Pascha nostrum*
[Rubric] *The Celebrant then says*
[Celebrant] The Lord be with you.
[People] **And also with you.**
[Rubric] *The Celebrant says one of the following Collects*
[Celebrant] Almighty God, who for our redemption gave your only- begotten Son to the death of the cross, and by his glorious resurrection delivered us from the power of our enemy: Grant us so to die daily to sin, that we may evermore live with him in the joy of his resurrection; through Jesus Christ your Son our Lord, who lives and reigns with you and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.
[People] **Amen.**
[Rubric] *or this*
[Celebrant] O God, who made this most holy night to shine with the glory of the Lord's resurrection: Stir up in your Church that Spirit of adoption which is given to us in Baptism, that we, being renewed both in body and mind, may worship you in sincerity and truth; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who lives and reigns with you, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.
[People] **Amen.**
[Rubric] *Epistle Romans 6:3-11*
[Rubric] *"Alleluia" may be sung and repeated.*
[Rubric] *Gospel Matthew 28:1-10*
[Rubric] *If a sermon or homily was not preached earlier, it follows here.*
[Rubric] *The Nicene Creed is not used at this service.*
[Rubric] *Holy Baptism, Confirmation, or the Renewal of Baptismal Vows may take place here.*
[Rubric] *The celebration continues with the Prayers of the People.*
